# Lead, 2026-09-28: the Mac's V4.1 router sets (prose, code, korean, threads) and hotlist-384.txt were traced
# from the dropped DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-Q3_K_M-engramQ8-tokembdBF16-attnQ8 file with ik c10fbbcc (their
# `# model` and `# build` lines). The engine runs the public Q3_K_M, and its oracle tree is ik-idxkey
# (db517b69 = c10fbbcc + the pre-RoPE index keys of ik#2507 + the sink fix of ik#2511). The warm re-sit
# needs held-out lists anyway (adaptres §5: the seed from each corpus's [0, 24576), prompt ids from
# [24576, ...)). So three traces of the public file with the profile's ik tree, each corpus's first 24,576
# ids, and a hot list from those three only.
# The term is read at the card's own n_l. n_expert is 384, so both lists rank all 384 experts of a layer and
# their first 384 are the same set by construction; the plans place spread:2668@2-39, 2668/38 = 70.2 a
# layer (70 or 71) [derived]. Layers 0-1 are always host, so they are out of the mean.
# Paper: the two lists differ by three things at once: the file (token embedding, attention and engram
# precision), the ik build (index keys), and the mix (hotlist-384 also learned on `threads`, from 50,000
# tokens a corpus). hotdiag found 26 % exact top-6 set equality per (layer, position) between the engine
# and the old prose trace (layer 0 alone 49/128). Exact set equality is much stricter than a top-70
# overlap of counts summed over 24,576 tokens, where near-tie swaps average out, so the band sits well
# above 26 %. Which of file and build carries the difference is router-attr.card's job, not this term's.
# Wall [derived]: 24,576 ids at the prose set's 66.5 tok/s = 6.2 min a corpus plus a cold read, 7-12 min
# each, three runs in one lease each; the hot-list build and the overlap seconds on the Mac.
kind: profile
question: how far does the hot list learned on the public file's routing, with the engine's ik tree,
  sit from hotlist-384 at the n_l the V4.1 plans place?
term: mean over layers 2-39 of |top70(pub-seed) ∩ top70(hotlist-384)| / 70, where pub-seed is the hot
  list built from prose-pub, code-pub and korean-pub (corpus-prose, -code, -korean ids [0, 24576),
  public Q3_K_M, ik-idxkey db517b69)
unit: ratio
predict: 0.60..0.85
condition: three runs, one lease each (router-trace.sh's lease_take):
  BLOOMERY_BOX_ENV='BLOOMERY_LEASE_CARD=docs/cards/router-pub.card' just trace-router prose --name
  prose-pub --chunk 2048 --max-tokens 24576, the same for code and korean; every manifest names the
  public first shard, build db517b69 and a complete trailer; then `just hotlist all hotlist-pub-seed.txt
  prose-pub code-pub korean-pub` (no lease); the overlap read on the Mac from the two list files
decide-in: the plans move to hotlist-pub-seed.txt; the re-sit draws prompt ids from [24576, ...);
  V4.1 hot-list rows measured since the requant was dropped are marked cross-file where cited
decide-below: the old list is a different list for the engine: every V4.1 hot-list row since the
  requant was dropped is re-read as a cross-file list, and the replays (ideaverify V1-V4) are re-run on
  the public sets before their numbers are cited
decide-above: the lists agree at n_l; the switch is still made (held-out by construction), no row is
  re-read
